'''Disarm''' is a debuff that makes affected units lose their currently equipped weapon.

==Mechanics==
Disarm works with slight differences depending on the unit affected:

*Afflicted enemy units that use firearms but can engage in melee combat have their weapons permanently removed or disabled and replaces them with a {{Weapon|Sheev}} if [[Grineer]] or {{Weapon|Prova}} if [[Corpus]], forcing said enemies to engage in close combat. If said enemies already have a secondary melee weapon, they will be forced to use that weapon.
*On ranged enemies without a secondary melee ability, Disarm permanently shuts down their weapons, making them incapable of attacking.
*Eximus units who are disarmed have their auras permanently disabled. 
**This will not work on melee eximus units, as melee units are inherently immune to disarm.
*When inflicted upon players, Disarm removes the weapon currently held by the Warframe. The player can still switch to any remaining weapons they may be carrying. The Warframe's disarmed weapon will be dropped on the ground, indicated by a yellow [[waypoint]], and can be retrieved. Players will not permanently lose their disarmed weapon should they fail to retrieve it before completing the mission.

Disarm does not work on [[Bosses]], nor on certain dedicated melee units, such as the [[Butcher]] or [[Scorpion]], who will retain their original moveset and melee capabilities. Certain melee units, such as [[Terra Trencher]]s, will permanently switch off of their special weapon, losing access to their unique melee combos in addition to significantly lowering their damage output. Light [[Infested]] humanoid units ([[Runner]]s, [[Leaper]]s) are ''literally'' disarmed, having both their arms removed, but can attack normally otherwise.

Disarm will not work on any targets with [[Overguard]] currently active, including players who have obtained Overguard from any source, such as {{WF|Rhino}}'s {{A|Iron Skin}}, {{WF|Kullervo}}'s {{A|Recompense}}, or {{WF|Dante}}'s {{A|Light Verse}}.
*Though this may be a bug, the following abilities seem to work through overguard. All other sources of Disarm do not disarm enemies hit by their abilities if they're overguarded, except for:
**{{Companion|Chesa Kubrow}} equipped with {{M|Neutralize}}
**{{WF|Mag}} equipped with {{M|Magnetized Discharge}}

Disarm will not work on {{Faction|Sentient}}, {{Faction|The Murmur}} and {{Faction|Anarchs|Anarch}} Dax units. If {{WF|Xaku}}'s {{A|Grasp of Lohk}} is used on them, they will still retain their weapons.

===Jam===
{{WF|Mesa}}'s {{A|Shooting Gallery}} and {{WF|Mag}}'s {{M|Counter Pulse}} '''jam''' enemy weapons, causing them to stop attacking and stand in place as they attempt to un-jam their weapon, providing a similar though temporarily effect to Disarm. {{A|Shooting Gallery}} also affects most melee attackers by stunning the unit in place instead, as they attempt to shake off the effects before continuing their approach. In [[Conclave]], jam abilities empty the victim's magazine, requiring them to reload to continue firing.

==Sources of Disarm==
*{{WF|Baruuk}}'s {{A|Desolate Hands}} and most attacks of {{A|Serene Storm}}
*{{WF|Khora}}'s {{A|Venari}} when set to Protect posture
*{{WF|Loki}}'s {{A|Radial Disarm}}
*{{WF|Mag}}'s {{M|Magnetized Discharge}}
*{{WF|Titania}}'s {{A|Spellbind}}
*{{WF|Xaku}}'s {{A|Grasp of Lohk}}
*{{Weapon|Halikar}} ({{Weapon|Halikar Wraith|Wraith}}) when thrown
**[[Grineer]] [[Drahk Master]]s, who use the Halikar
*{{M|Disarming Purity}} mod for the {{Weapon|Panthera}}/{{Weapon|Panthera Prime}}
*[[Chesa Kubrow]]'s {{M|Neutralize}}
*{{M|Repo Audit}} for [[Hound (Companion)|Hounds]]
*{{Focus|Zenurik}}'s {{Focus|Disarming Sling}}

