'''Scyotid''' is {{WF|Oraxia}}'s [[Signature Weapon|signature]] [[Thrown|throwing knives]]. Dealing {{D|Toxin}} damage, its [[Alternate Fire]] throws a snare that binds and pulls in enemies.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Toxin}} damage.
*Primary fire has innate 1.6 meter [[Punch Through]].
*[[Alternate Fire]] throws a webbed snare that damages, paralyzes for '''~6''' seconds, and groups up to '''8''' enemies within '''15''' meters.
**Number of pulled enemies is multiplied by [[Multishot]].
**Radius is '''not''' affected by {{M|Fulmination}} ({{M|Primed Fulmination|Primed}}).
**Damage is '''not''' affected by mods, nor does it combine with or inflict modded elements.
**Consumes 4 ammo per shot.
*Innate {{Pol|Naramon}} polarity.

{{Advantages|}}
{{Disadvantages|
*Projectiles have travel time.}}

==Acquisition==
{{Acquisition|header=no|Scyotid's main and component blueprints can be obtained from [[Isleweaver]] in [[Duviri]]. Access requires completion of [[The Hex (Quest)|The Hex]] Quest.

Alternatively, Scyotid's blueprints can be purchased from [[File:IconDuviriAcrithis.png|30x30px]][[Acrithis]] or [[Dominus Thrax]] in the [[Dormizone]], using {{Resource|Scuttler Husk}} awarded from Isleweaver. Each component blueprint requires 12 {{#invoke:Tooltips|icon|Scuttler Husk|Resources}} and the main blueprint requires 48 {{#invoke:Tooltips|icon|Scuttler Husk|Resources}}, totaling 96 {{#invoke:Tooltips|icon|Scuttler Husk|Resources}} Scuttler Husks for the complete set.}}

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

==Notes==
*As the alternate fire is unable to crit, repeated uses will build stacks of {{Arcane|Secondary Enervate}} without consuming them.

==Trivia==
*The Scyotid name is based on the [[wikipedia:Scytodidae|Scytodidae]] which a family of spiders known for lobbing venom coated silk onto their prey which fits in with the weapon innate toxin damages and being a throwable weapon.
**The "barbs" projectiles might be a nod to how some Tarantulas defend themselves by sending harpoon shaped barbs in the air to blind any threats that might want to eat them.

